/-!
# Lifting compact objects along a finite localization

Let `L : T ⥤ T'` be an exact functor between triangulated categories with direct sums, left
adjoint to a fully faithful functor `G` which commutes with direct sums, and suppose that the
kernel of `L` is generated by a set of compact objects `K i` of `T` in the sense of
[Stacks, Tag 09IR]: an object right orthogonal to every shift of every `K i` lies in the image of
`G`. If `T` is compactly generated by a nonempty family, then for every compact object `P` of `T'`
there is a compact object `c` of `T` with

`L c ≅ P ⊕ P[1]`.

This is the categorical content of [Stacks, Tag 08EK] (Thomason–Trobaugh, Neeman): in the source
`T = D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` for `X` affine, `T' = D_QCoh(𝒪_U)` for a quasi-compact open `U ⊆ X`, `L` is
restriction and the `K i` are Koszul complexes.

## The argument

* `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.exists_fac_triangEnvelope_of_localizingClosure` (the
  factorization lemma of Neeman): a morphism from a compact object of `T` into an object of the
  localizing subcategory generated by the `K i` factors through the triangulated envelope of a
  finite direct sum of the `K i`. The object is a derived colimit of cell attachments inside the
  localizing subcategory ([Stacks, Tag 09SN]), a morphism from a compact object factors through a
  term ([Stacks, Tag 094A]), and then through a finite stage ([Stacks, Tag 09SP]).
* `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.exists_roof`: every morphism `L c₁ ⟶ L c₂` between images of
  compact objects is `L g' ∘ (L s)⁻¹` for compact `c`, `s : c ⟶ c₁` with `L s` invertible and
  `g' : c ⟶ c₂`. The obstruction to lifting is a morphism from `c₁` into the cone of the unit at
  `c₂`, an object of the kernel of `L`, which is the localizing subcategory generated by the
  `K i`; factoring it through a compact object of the kernel and taking the fibre removes it.
* The images `L c` of compact objects form a triangulated subcategory, so the objects that are
  direct summands of such images form a thick one; it contains the generators `L Gⱼ`, and by
  [Stacks, Tag 09SR] the compact objects of `T'` are the thick envelope of those.
* Thomason's trick: if `P ⊕ C ≅ L c₀`, the cone of the projection of `P ⊕ C` onto `C` is
  `P[1] ⊕ P`, by the octahedral axiom, and it is the image of a compact object.

## What the roof lemma does not give: the tensor clause of Tag 08EH

`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.exists_roof` is the first assertion of [Stacks, Tag 08EH] — the
roof `E ← E₁ → E'` with `E₁` compact and `E₁ ⟶ E` restricting to an isomorphism on the open. It
is **not** the second assertion, "moreover we can assume `E₁ = E ⊗^𝐋 I` for some perfect complex
`I` on `X`", and that difference is load-bearing rather than cosmetic.

In the source the tensor presentation is used in exactly two places, and in both of them for one
purpose only: to carry *cohomological support* from `E` to `E₁`. In [Stacks, Tag 08EK] it is
"`C' = C_s ⊗^𝐋 I`, hence the nullity of `g_j² id_{C_s}` implies the same thing for `C'`; thus
`C'` is supported on `T` as well", and in [Stacks, Tag 09IM] it is "we can replace `Q` by
`Q ⊗^𝐋 I` (still supported on `T ∩ V`)". Support is the only thing the clause buys, and it is
the only thing the roof above cannot supply: `exists_roof` builds its source as the fibre of a
morphism `c₁ ⟶ Z` with `Z` merely in the triangulated envelope of a finite direct sum of the
chosen generators `K i` of the kernel of `L`. In the geometric instance those generators are
Koszul complexes on the equations cutting out the complement of the open, so `Z` is supported on
that complement, and the fibre is known to be supported only on the union of the support of `c₁`
with it — not on the support of `c₁`.

So the lemmas here give the whole of 08EK and 08EH for objects with no support condition, and
`Stacks.Duality.QcqsGeneration.exists_isCompactObject_restrict_iso_biprod_shift` is that
instance. A consumer that needs the *supported* forms — [Stacks, Tag 08EK] as stated, and
[Stacks, Tag 09IM] — has two routes, neither of which is in the library:

* [Stacks, Tag 08DD], the identification `colim_e Hom(I_e, E) ≅ H⁰(U, E)` for the extended
  alternating Čech objects `I_e`, which is what produces the tensor presentation in the first
  place. **This is now available**, for an affine scheme and an object with quasi-coherent
  cohomology, as `Koszul.DerivedSystem.bijective_cohomologyComparison` in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Perfect/KoszulCohomologyBijective.lean`; its `@[stacks 08DD]`
  registration is owned elsewhere, so it carries none. Both uses the source makes of the tensor
  clause — in 08EK and in 09IM — are at an affine scheme, so the affine hypothesis is the right
  one, and in both the second argument has quasi-coherent cohomology.
* or running the instantiation inside `D_{QCoh,T}` instead of `D_QCoh`, where the support
  condition is carried by the category and nothing has to be propagated. That category is built,
  with its triangulated structure and its direct sums, as
  `Stacks.Duality.QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory` in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration/SupportedQuasiCoherent.lean`; what is
  missing is its compact generating family, which is [Stacks, Tag 0A9A] together with
  [Stacks, Tag 0A9B]. With 08DD available this route is no longer needed.

